#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Quality-Guide.rst:17
msgid ""
"Code quality practices help ROS package maintainers build software that is "
"reliable, secure, maintainable, and easier to validate. This article "
"provides guidance for improving package quality through analysis, testing, "
"implementation patterns, and other practices that support robust ROS "
"development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Quality-Guide.rst:25
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Quality-Guide.rst:27
msgid ""
"This page gives guidance about how to improve the software quality of ROS 2 "
"packages, focusing on more specific areas than the Quality Practices section "
"of the :doc:`Developer Guide <../Developer-Guide>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-code/Quality-Guide.rst:29
msgid ""
"The sections below intend to address ROS 2 core, application and ecosystem "
"packages and the core client libraries, C++ and Python. The solutions "
"presented are motivated by design and implementation considerations to "
"improve quality attributes like \"Reliability\", \"Security\", "
"\"Maintainability\", \"Determinism\", etc. which relate to non-functional "
"requirements."
msgstr ""

